{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_22","type":"agent_message","text":"The first-pass evidence already falsifies the proposed fixed-degree scale: published work proves `rc(G(n,d)) = Θ(log n)` w.h.p. for every fixed `d ≥ 3`, while `n/d` is linear. I’ve frozen the Phase 1 direction budget around (1) auditing that contradiction, (2) extracting the best fixed-degree proof machinery, and (3) separating fixed versus growing degree regimes."}}
