{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_82","type":"agent_message","text":"The full-text review confirms a sharper and very different landscape than the prompt suggests: the meaningful open direction is closeness to the diameter, not closeness to `n/d`. A 2012 paper even conjectures `rc(G)=diam(G)` w.h.p. for random regular graphs; later work establishes only the correct order, including the cubic case. I’m now checking post-2017 citations for any newer resolution before finalizing the catalog."}}
