{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_110","type":"agent_message","text":"Completed the resource-finding phase and created the completion marker.\n\nThe decisive finding is that the stated hypothesis is false for fixed \\(d\\ge3\\): published results establish\n\\[\nrc(G(n,d))=\\Theta(\\log n)\\quad\\text{w.h.p.},\n\\]\nwhereas \\(\\lceil n/d\\rceil=\\Theta(n)\\). The likely confusion is that \\(3n/(\\delta+1)+3\\) is a worst-case universal upper bound, not a random-regular lower bound. A literature-supported replacement is to investigate \\(rc(G)=\\operatorname{diam}(G)+O(1)\\), or initially \\(rc(G)=(1+o(1))\\operatorname{diam}(G)\\). See [Dudek–Frieze–Tsourakakis](https://arxiv.org/abs/1311.2299) and [Molloy](https://www.combinatorics.org/ojs/index.php/eljc/article/download/v24i3p49/pdf).\n\nArtifacts:\n\n- [Literature review](/workspaces/tight-bounds-on-the-rainbow-connection-8c65/literature_review.md)\n- [Resource catalog](/workspaces/tight-bounds-on-the-rainbow-connection-8c65/resources.md)\n- [Direction scoring and pruning](/workspaces/tight-bounds-on-the-rainbow-connection-8c65/planning.md)\n- [Downloaded-paper index](/workspaces/tight-bounds-on-the-rainbow-connection-8c65/papers/README.md)\n- [Computational tools](/workspaces/tight-bounds-on-the-rainbow-connection-8c65/code/README.md)\n- [Phase handoff state](/workspaces/tight-bounds-on-the-rainbow-connection-8c65/STATE.md)\n- [Completion marker](/workspaces/tight-bounds-on-the-rainbow-connection-8c65/.resource_finder_complete)\n\nNine source PDFs and 47 reading chunks passed strict validation. The two supplied arXiv IDs were read fully but excluded because they concern quantum non-classicality and digital ecosystems, respectively. The paper-finder service was unavailable, so the structured review workflow used arXiv, OpenAlex, publisher sources, and citation chaining instead."}}
